<h1>Industrial Air Compressors</h1>
<div class="row">
	<div class="col-md-12">
		<p>
		Industrial air compressors are designed for manufacturing and commercial operations who require a continuous supply of compressed air. These systems are designed for 24/7 operation and can run Industrial compressors come in many different configurations that can be customized to your operation.
		</p>
		<p>
		The most common style is an electric oil-injected rotary screw compressor. Screw compressors are designed for continuous-duty 100% load capacity. They achieve this by utilizing two rotating screws that spin counter to eachother which compresses air.
		</p>
		<p>
		We carry industrial air compressors for sale between 3hp and 500hp from Ingersoll Rand and Chicago Pneumatic. We invite you to stop by our showroom today. Our staff can wire any compressor in our testing bay, letting you see the compressor operate before you buy.
		</p>
	</div>
	<div class="col-sm-12">
		<div class="row">
			<div class="col-sm-12">
				<h3>Ingersoll Rand Industrial Rotary Screw Air Compressors</h3>
				<img class="float-end" alt="Ingersoll Rand" src="../images/site/ingersoll-rand.gif">
				<p>
					Ingersoll Rand industrial air compressors are some of the highest quality rotary compressors on the market. Their trademark model has been the "SSR" series which stands for Serviceability, Simplicity and Reliability. IR's SSR UP6 series has been one of the most popular selling rotary screw compressors for the past two decades.
				</p>

				<p>
					A large part of the Ingersoll value comes from its many design innovations. Their cabinet enclosure includes a panel pre filter which cleans filters the air prior to entering the air compressor. Ingersoll Rand designed the speed, torque and operating characteristics to perfectly match the load of the compressor.
				</p>

				<p>
					Ingersoll rand offers single phase screw compressors in a 5hp and 7.5hp configuration. Tank mount rotary screw air compressors and tankless air compressors are both available. IR has large industrial air compressors up to 500+HP that can be customized to your facility. Regardless of your compressed air requirement, Ingersoll Rand has a solution that meets your needs.
				</p>
